---
// src/pages/cookie-policy.astro
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Navbar from '../components/global/Navbar.astro';
import Footer from '../components/global/Footer.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Cookie Policy | ZetaLogix">
    <Navbar />
    
    <main class="pt-32 bg-brand-dark text-slate-300 min-h-screen relative overflow-hidden">
        <div class="absolute top-0 left-1/2 -translate-x-1/2 w-[800px] h-[400px] bg-brand-accent/5 rounded-full blur-[120px] pointer-events-none"></div>

        <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6 py-12 relative z-10">
            <div class="border-b border-white/10 pb-8 mb-12">
                <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold text-white font-heading mb-4">Cookie Policy</h1>
                <p class="text-sm text-brand-accent font-mono uppercase tracking-wider">Last Updated: August 1, 2026</p>
            </div>

            <div class="space-y-10 text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-400">
                <p>
                    This Tracking Policy clarifies how <span class="text-white font-semibold">ZetaLogix</span> applies cookies, modular cache systems, and telemetry tracking arrays to provide high-fidelity navigation and optimize our online performance metrics.
                </p>

                <div class="space-y-4">
                    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white font-heading flex items-center gap-3">
                        <span class="text-brand-accent font-mono text-base">01.</span> Understanding Cookies
                    </h2>
                    <p>
                        Cookies are minimal, temporary cryptographic text arrays deployed within your access terminal when you trigger an entry request to our domains. They track telemetry parameters, allowing server-side components to dynamically remember your interface settings, drop-down configurations, and profile indicators to optimize site response speeds.
                    </p>
                </div>

                <div class="space-y-6">
                    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white font-heading flex items-center gap-3">
                        <span class="text-brand-accent font-mono text-base">02.</span> How We Deploy Tracking Classes
                    </h2>
                    
                    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
                        <div class="bg-[#0a0f1d] border border-white/5 rounded-xl p-5">
                            <h3 class="text-white font-bold mb-2 flex items-center gap-2">
                                <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-brand-accent"></span> Essential Architecture
                            </h3>
                            <p class="text-sm text-slate-400">Mandatory arrays used to safely navigate components, protect modal input payloads, and retain form status values when moving through multi-tier pages.</p>
                        </div>

                        <div class="bg-[#0a0f1d] border border-white/5 rounded-xl p-5">
                            <h3 class="text-white font-bold mb-2 flex items-center gap-2">
                                <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-purple-400"></span> Performance & Metrics
                            </h3>
                            <p class="text-sm text-slate-400">Aggregated tracking structures that trace interface engagement, pinpoint loading bottlenecks, and calculate global entry channels without storing individual identifiers.</p>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="space-y-4">
                    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white font-heading flex items-center gap-3">
                        <span class="text-brand-accent font-mono text-base">03.</span> User Configuration & Management
                    </h2>
                    <p>
                        Users retain permanent structural control over cookie distribution. You can configure your local browser to reject tracking flags entirely or notify you before deployment. Please note that turning off analytical flags is fully compatible with our platform, but disabling essential architectures may cause modal triggers or menu layouts to load with incomplete operational functions.
                    </p>
                </div>

                <div class="bg-slate-800/20 border border-white/5 rounded-2xl p-6 text-center">
                    <p class="text-sm text-slate-300">
                        If you have inquiries regarding our cookie tracking behaviors, contact our systems team at <a href="mailto:info@zetalogix.com" class="text-brand-accent font-bold hover:underline">info@zetalogix.com</a>.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </main>

    <Footer />
</BaseLayout>